Ritemark Build System: making the VS Code fork build and run correctly
Consolidates old patches: 008 (jschardet), 009 (microphone), 013 (integrity check)
Also delegates the microphone Permissions-Policy feature to webview iframes
(required since Electron 39 enforces iframe media policy; fixes voice dictation, GH #116)
Sprint 135: rebased onto VS Code 1.142.0 (app.ts: upstream's permission handler now takes webContents and
lists 'media' for the core window; this patch still adds it to the webview list)
Sprint 135 E5: the packaging step that prepares the built-in Copilot's SDK skips when the packaged Copilot has none
(a build from source strips it through .moduleignore's @github/copilot/**; Ritemark deletes the built-in Copilot after)
Sprint 135 E5: the build's commit reader follows a .git file ("gitdir: ..."), so product.json names the commit in release
worktrees and CI; from 1.142 an app without one reads node modules from node_modules/, not node_modules.asar
Sprint 135 E5: the commit is RITEMARK_SOURCE_COMMIT when the build sets it (Ritemark's source commit, as in the provenance)
